# Blackjack

Blackjack **engine and accounting are frozen**. Presentation may change only when explicitly requested, using the canonical Tabletop components.

## Phase sequence

`TABLE_SETUP → BETTING → PLAYING → PAYOUT → ROUND_COMPLETE → BETTING`

No backward transitions and no phase skipping. Insurance is a Bank-triggered window during PLAYING (not a phase) and settles independently during PAYOUT.

## Roles and privacy

- Owner: invite, assign Bank/Dealer, rename, distribute jetons, save/close, switch games at safe boundaries
- Bank/Dealer: start betting, deal, Insurance window, enter payout, settle boxes/Insurance, next round; optional Card Assist on Dealer hand and Player boxes
- Player: own boxes only; bet/retract in BETTING; Double/Split in PLAYING; Insurance while window open; Card Assist only on own selected box
- Player never sees another Player’s boxes or the Dealer Open/Limited toggle
- Bank sees all active boxes
- Screen choice is `selectTableBoard()` from snapshot flags only (`isDealer`, `isSeatedPlayer`, `isOwner`, game, phase)

## Boxes

- One felt box instance per active engine box; never aggregate by Player
- Split maps to existing engine boxes (`isSplit` / offshoot); UI never fabricates hands
- Do not invent empty seated Players as active wager boxes
- `BlackjackBoxStage` ordering: highest box number on the LEFT; Box 1 is the rightmost centre anchor (`[BOX 3] [BOX 2] [BOX 1]`)

## Canonical Dealer Tabletop

- `BlackjackTableSurface` is the shared physical felt for Dealer and Player in **every** Blackjack phase (CSS/SVG markings — never a screenshot background)
- Felt/table is the permanent base; Dealer bank, Setup joined marks, box stage, and Payout bars overlay it
- Table name is printed on the felt (`data-felt-name`) — full name visible, never ellipsised on ordinary names
- PhaseDisplay stacks title then instruction (never side-by-side)
- `BlackjackDealerTable` mounts `BlackjackTableSurface` for **every** phase including `TABLE_SETUP`
- `BankTable` is a thin adapter that mounts `BlackjackDealerTable`
- Owner/Dealer at BJ `TABLE_SETUP` selects `BLACKJACK_DEALER` — **not** `PHASE_ZERO_DEALER` / PhaseZero ledger

### Phase presentation matrix (Dealer)

| Phase | Presentation |
|---|---|
| TABLE_SETUP | Compact `JoinedPlayerMark` indicators (`PLAYER JOINED` + available jetons) — never READY, never MAIN BET, never spreadsheet rows |
| BETTING / PLAYING / INSURANCE | `BlackjackBoxStage` physical box positions (shared with Player) — never full-width ledger bars |
| PAYOUT / ROUND_COMPLETE | Full-width `DealerLedgerRow` settlement bars only |

- Zero seated Players → zero joined marks + empty copy `No players have joined yet.` + `Invite a Player to begin.`
- Invited/pending identities are not seated Players; Bank/Dealer membership is not a Player row
- Never put available balance under MAIN BET; never show MAIN BET until a real box wager exists
- Compact Dealer position always present (quiet reserved height when no cards)
- Unresolved payout: one horizontal four-action group `LOST | TIE | BJ | WIN` (accessible Lost / Stand-off / Blackjack / Won); never a 2×2 grid
- Insurance settle stays separate: `INS LOST | INS WON`
- Phase changes may alter labels, instruction, values, and legal controls — not felt / box-stage / Dealer geometry

## Dock matrix (product labels)

| Phase | Primary | Secondary |
|---|---|---|
| TABLE_SETUP | START BETTING | ADD PLAYER |
| BETTING | DEAL CARDS | ADD PLAYER |
| PLAYING | ENTER PAYOUT | OPEN INSURANCE |
| Insurance open | ENTER PAYOUT | CLOSE INSURANCE |
| Payout unresolved | START BETTING (disabled) + result controls | — |
| Payout resolved | START BETTING | — |

Do not show `CLOSE BETTING` or `START NEXT ROUND` as normal UI wording. Controls derive from `blackjack-phase-controls.ts`. Use existing commands only.

## Player Betting presentation

- Same `BlackjackTableSurface` + `BlackjackBoxStage` as Dealer during Betting / Playing / Insurance
- Permanent bottom AVAILABLE + jeton tray in every phase
- Per-box retract × during BETTING when MAIN > 0 (`placeBet` mode `RETRACT`); accessible name `Retract Box {n} wager`
- No second full-width dock RETRACT when × is canonical
- Primary wager chips use shared `ChipStack` lg (~46–56px at 390×844); Insurance secondary smaller
- Doubled boxes show `2×` without inventing another box
- Box stage Y stays in the lower ~62–68% of the felt; do not move Box 1 upward between phases

## Card Assist

Display-only. Player edits own selected box; Dealer edits Dealer hand and may correct Player boxes. Never settles, chooses winners, changes balances, or advances phases.
